    "html_url": "https://github.com/romaine-life/kill-me/commit/0855dbc168a68a37f12b20db7b59b91364644bdd",
    "message": "feat: make mobile data entry first-class (keypads, Log in bottom nav, safe area)\n\nAudited every tab at 375px. The logging flow was built desktop-first; this\nlands the highest-impact mobile data-entry fixes:\n\n- Weight/reps/sets inputs were type=\"text\", so phones popped the full QWERTY\n  keyboard. Add inputMode (decimal for weight, numeric for reps/sets) so the\n  numeric keypad shows, and bump their touch height (py-2 -\u003e py-3).\n- The Log tab was missing from the mobile bottom nav (buried in the hamburger).\n  Surface it centered — the primary daily action — for admins; public visitors\n  still see the same four tabs.\n- Add viewport-fit=cover + env(safe-area-inset-bottom) padding so the bottom nav\n  isn't tucked under the home indicator on notched phones, and pad the scroll\n  area so the last row of content clears the fixed nav.",
    "node_id": "C_kwDORV0mMdoAKDA4NTVkYmMxNjhhNjhhMzdmMTJiMjBkYjdiNTliOTEzNjQ2NDRiZGQ",
